{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KsGCXor2r5GLf5eJZQ4weo","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# agent-evals\n2\t\n3\tA small harness that runs coding agents on short tasks and keeps everything a\n4\trun produced, so the runs can be graded and compared later. It lives in\n5\t`~/evals/agent-evals` on the eval Mac.\n6\t\n7\t`./run.sh <task> <lane> [rep]` copies `tasks/<task>/` into a scratch folder in\n8\t`/tmp`, runs the lane's agent there with `tasks/<task>.prompt`, and writes the\n9\trun folder `runs/<task>-<lane>-r<rep>/`:\n10\t\n11\t- `prompt.txt`, `agent.log` (the agent's JSON event stream), `agent.err`,\n12\t  `meta.json` (exit code, seconds);\n13\t- `final.txt`, the agent's last message, for the Codex lanes;\n14\t- `answer.json`, written by `check_answer.py`: the final answer the graders\n15\t  read (from `final.txt` for Codex, from the event stream for Kimi).\n16\t\n17\tLanes:\n18\t\n19\t- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n20\t- `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the\n21\t  macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real\n22\t  home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in\n23\t  `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens.\n24\t\n25\tCodex logs in with an API key from the environment (`CODEX_API_KEY`), so it\n26\tneeds nothing from the home folder.\n27\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a90e5235-fa31-483f-afde-7d9b61e91d4f","uuid":"98b43920-e25e-44d8-95f2-fc92321f3697","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:55:18.645Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-njM7dG/README.md","content":"# agent-evals\n\nA small harness that runs coding agents on short tasks and keeps everything a\nrun produced, so the runs can be graded and compared later. It lives in\n`~/evals/agent-evals` on the eval Mac.\n\n`./run.sh <task> <lane> [rep]` copies `tasks/<task>/` into a scratch folder in\n`/tmp`, runs the lane's agent there with `tasks/<task>.prompt`, and writes the\nrun folder `runs/<task>-<lane>-r<rep>/`:\n\n- `prompt.txt`, `agent.log` (the agent's JSON event stream), `agent.err`,\n  `meta.json` (exit code, seconds);\n- `final.txt`, the agent's last message, for the Codex lanes;\n- `answer.json`, written by `check_answer.py`: the final answer the graders\n  read (from `final.txt` for Codex, from the event stream for Kimi).\n\nLanes:\n\n- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n- `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the\n  macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real\n  home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in\n  `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens.\n\nCodex logs in with an API key from the environment (`CODEX_API_KEY`), so it\nneeds nothing from the home folder.\n","numLines":27,"startLine":1,"totalLines":27}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KsGCXor2r5GLf5eJZQ4weo","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
