{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FygMbrRSPSxM8jXqK9AT6Y","type":"tool_result","content":"syntax ok\n M README.md\n M run.sh\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\nindex 9d81ca7..a6cf9b1 100644\n--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -17,10 +17,15 @@ run folder `runs/<task>-<lane>-r<rep>/`:\n Lanes:\n \n - `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n+- `codex-sandboxed`: the same Codex run under `sandbox/agent.sb`, like `kimi`.\n+  Codex gets a scratch `CODEX_HOME` with copies of `~/.codex/config.toml` and\n+  `auth.json`, and writes its last message to a scratch folder in `/tmp`, which\n+  is copied into `final.txt` after the sandbox exits.\n - `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the\n   macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real\n   home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in\n   `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens.\n \n-Codex logs in with an API key from the environment (`CODEX_API_KEY`), so it\n-needs nothing from the home folder.\n+The `codex` lane reads `~/.codex` in place. `codex-sandboxed` can't reach the\n+real home, so it copies `config.toml` and `auth.json` into its scratch\n+`CODEX_HOME`. Codex's `CODEX_API_KEY` from the environment is passed through.\ndiff --git a/run.sh b/run.sh\nindex c41ad67..a9be7de 100755\n--- a/run.sh\n+++ b/run.sh\n@@ -1,7 +1,8 @@\n #!/usr/bin/env bash\n # usage: run.sh <task> <lane> [rep]\n-# lanes: codex   Codex CLI, unsandboxed\n-#        kimi    Kimi Code under sandbox/agent.sb (no reading or writing the real home), scratch HOME\n+# lanes: codex            Codex CLI, unsandboxed\n+#        codex-sandboxed  the same Codex run under sandbox/agent.sb (no reading or writing the real home)\n+#        kimi             Kimi Code under sandbox/agent.sb (no reading or writing the real home), scratch HOME\n set -u\n D=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\n T=$1; A=$2; REP=${3:-1}\n@@ -24,9 +25,28 @@ kimi_run() {\n   local rc=$?; rm -rf \"$SH\"; return $rc\n }\n \n+# codex-sandboxed: codex_run under sandbox/agent.sb, like kimi. Codex gets a scratch HOME and CODEX_HOME holding copies of\n+# config.toml and auth.json. -o goes to a scratch folder in /tmp, not the run folder: inside the sandbox a write under the\n+# real home is denied, and codex exits 0 anyway, so the copy-out happens after sandbox-exec returns.\n+codexsb_run() {\n+  local REAL=\"$HOME\" SH CS CH rc\n+  SH=$(mktemp -d /tmp/chome-XXXXXX); CS=$(mktemp -d /tmp/cout-XXXXXX); CH=\"$SH/.codex\"; mkdir -p \"$CH\"\n+  cp \"$REAL/.codex/config.toml\" \"$REAL/.codex/auth.json\" \"$CH/\"\n+  ( cd \"$W\" && export HOME=\"$SH\" && sandbox-exec -D HOME=\"$REAL\" -f \"$D/sandbox/agent.sb\" \\\n+      env CODEX_HOME=\"$CH\" timeout $TO codex exec --skip-git-repo-check --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox -C \"$W\" --json \\\n+      -o \"$CS/final.txt\" \"$P\" < /dev/null > \"$R/agent.log\" 2> \"$R/agent.err\" )\n+  rc=$?\n+  if [ -f \"$CS/final.txt\" ]; then cp \"$CS/final.txt\" \"$R/final.txt\"; fi\n+  rm -rf \"$SH\" \"$CS\"\n+  if [ ! -s \"$R/final.txt\" ]; then echo \"warning: no final.txt in $R (see agent.err)\" >&2; fi\n+  if grep -q \"Operation not permitted\" \"$R/agent.err\"; then echo \"warning: a write was denied, see $R/agent.err\" >&2; fi\n+  return $rc\n+}\n+\n start=$(date +%s)\n case $A in\n   codex) codex_run;;\n+  codex-sandboxed) codexsb_run;;\n   kimi)  kimi_run;;\n   *) echo \"unknown lane $A\"; exit 2;;\n esac","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a90e5235-fa31-483f-afde-7d9b61e91d4f","uuid":"d231c0b2-eed6-4c2e-98c9-8439d415979b","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:55:48.519Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"syntax ok\n M README.md\n M run.sh\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\nindex 9d81ca7..a6cf9b1 100644\n--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -17,10 +17,15 @@ run folder `runs/<task>-<lane>-r<rep>/`:\n Lanes:\n \n - `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), uns